<title>USA: U.S. propane stocks fall 2.9 million.</title>
<headline>U.S. propane stocks fall 2.9 million.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. propane inventories fell 2.9 million in the week to 34.4 million barrels but stayed above year-ago levels, according to the Energy Information Administration Wednesday report.</p>
<p>In the week ended January 24, propane in the Gulf Coast fell 1.9 million barrels to 18.3 million, about 3.1 million barrels above year-ago levels, the report said.</p>
<p>The Midwest fell 700,000 to 10.7 million, two million below year-ago levels. The East Coast dropped about 300,000 to 4.1 million, about 1.9 million above year-ago levels.</p>
<p>--((Laney Salisbury, New York Energy Desk 1212 859-1631))</p>
